                  <provenance type="#s l"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_122">Canterbury, Kent.
                        Benedictine abbey of St Augustine (originally of St Peter and St Paul)</orgName><p>Probably formed one volume with Selden Supra 26. One quire of
                        eight leaves.</p><p>Additions to the Kalendar made at St Augustine's in s.
                        xiii2: April 27 'Veneratio'; St Augustine's grading of feasts, as in St
                        John's Cambr. MS. 262 (pr. Wormald, Benedictine calendars after
                        1100).</p><p>The additions are probably by W. de S. Clara, and this was part
                        of Selden Supra 26, which formerly contained 'Tabule astronomice cum
                        Kalendario. compotus'.</p></provenance>
